.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt BMAKE-IT 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bmake-it
.Nd BSD make build system for C and C++: workspaces, frameworks and modules
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm bmake
.Op Ar target ...
.Op Ar variable Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a set of
.Xr make 1
include files for building C, C++, lex and yacc sources on macOS, Linux,
.Fx ,
.Nx
and Windows.
A makefile states what it is and includes the file for that role; sources,
frameworks and modules are found by convention.
.Pp
There are three levels.
A
.Em workspace
contains frameworks.
A
.Em framework
is a directory whose makefile sets
.Va PREREQS ,
and contains modules.
A
.Em module
is a directory named
.Pa *.m
that builds one library or one program, or
.Pa *.tst
for a test module.
.Pp
Output goes to
.Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa / ,
where
.Ar KEY
is
.Ar os Ns - Ns Ar arch Ns Op - Ns Ar toolchain Ns Op - Ns Ar abi
with defaults omitted, so builds for different targets sit side by side.
.Ss Files to include
.Bl -column "mk.workspace.mk" "description" -offset indent
.It Sy Role Ta Sy Page
.It workspace Ta Xr mk.workspace.mk 5
.It framework Ta Xr mk.framework.mk 5
.It library module Ta Xr mk.lib.mk 5
.It program module Ta Xr mk.prog.mk 5
.It test module Ta Xr mk.tst.mk 5
.El
.Ss Files the roles read themselves
.Bl -tag -width "mk.constraint-axis.mk" -offset indent
.It Xr mk.common.mk 5
target selection, target key, flags, sanitizers,
.Cm run
.It Xr mk.local.mk 5
per-level hook files
.It Xr mk.constraints.mk 5 , Xr mk.constraint-axis.mk 5
.Va PLATFORMS
and
.Va TOOLCHAINS
.It Xr mk.skipped.mk 5
what an excluded module or framework does instead
.It Xr mk.requires.mk 5
.Va REQUIRES
.It Xr mk.delayload.mk 5
.Va DELAYLOAD
.It Xr mk.test.mk 5 , Xr mk.crosstest.mk 5
.Cm test ,
locally or on a runner
.It Xr mk.atf.mk 5 , Xr mk.atfbmk.mk 5
finding or building ATF
.It Xr mk.docs.mk 5
.Cm docs
.It Xr mk.help.mk 5
.Cm help
.It Xr mk.toolchain.llvm.mk 5 , Xr mk.toolchain.gcc.mk 5 , Xr mk.toolchain.msvc.mk 5
compiler bundles
.It Xr mk.vcvarsall.mk 5
finding MSVC without a developer prompt
.It Xr mk.paths.5
where tools are looked for, per host
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "MAKESYSPATH"
.It Ev MAKESYSPATH
Where
.Xr make 1
finds the include files: Bmake It's
.Pa mk/
directory, then the system's.
.Pa scripts/install-env.sh
sets it, and
.Ev MANPATH
for these pages, in your shell's startup file.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "docs/spec/"
.It Pa mk/
the include files
.It Pa scripts/
helpers they call
.It Pa docs/spec/
the design, with the reasons behind what these pages state
.It Pa project-model/
the requirements and decisions
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A workspace with one framework, one library and one program:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
myws/makefile              PARENT_WS=
                           \&.include <mk.workspace.mk>
myws/Fw/makefile           PREREQS=
                           \&.include <mk.framework.mk>
myws/Fw/libgreet.m/makefile
                           \&.include <mk.lib.mk>
myws/Fw/libgreet.m/src/greet.c
myws/Fw/hello.m/makefile   LIBS=greet
                           \&.include <mk.prog.mk>
myws/Fw/hello.m/src/main.c
.Ed
.Pp
Build it, for another toolchain, and run the program:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ bmake
$ bmake TOOLCHAIN=gcc
$ bmake run PROGRAM=hello
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1 ,
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.framework.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.lib.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.tst.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.workspace.mk 5 ,
.Xr mdoc 7
